# Brewlette

Beer roulette for an iPad behind a bar. Fun bar toy — not enterprise software.

## Stack (do not change without asking)

- React + Vite + JavaScript
- HTML Canvas wheel; CSS design tokens in `src/styles/`
- `localStorage` via `src/utils/storage.js` only
- Static site only — **no** backend, auth, API, DB, Firebase, Next.js

## Architecture

Prefer the existing layout: `components/`, `hooks/useBeerList.js`, `utils/{storage,random,wheel}.js`, `data/defaultBeers.js`.

Keep wheel math in `wheel.js`; keep crypto selection in `random.js`. **Pick the winner first, then animate** — never use animation position as randomness.

## UX invariants

- Wheel-first Spin Mode; subtle Edit entry (no admin chrome on the wheel)
- Touch targets ≥ 44px; hover is optional, never required
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (shorter spin; still show the result)
- Empty / 1-beer / corrupt storage / long names must not break the UI
- Optional “Remove this beer” after a spin — never auto-remove

## Design

Warm, slightly dark, playful bar aesthetic. Tokens in `tokens.css` — no one-off colors/spacing. Distinctive display type for brand + result. Avoid SaaS dashboards, rustic wood kitsch, neon glow spam.

